  "goodToKnow": "Der Klient (die Klientin) is a client, mainly of lawyers, counsellors, social workers or therapists. For shops and most businesses, German uses der Kunde. Lawyers also say der Mandant. It's a weak noun: den Klienten. Die Klientel is a clientele or, in politics, a party's core voters: Klientelpolitik means policies favouring one interest group. Stressed on the last syllable: kli-ENT. Plural: die Klienten."
